  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (adding O.C.G.A. 20-2-1187(b)): (b)(1) Each local board of education and other public school governing body shall implement a weapon detection system and shall adopt policies, rules, regulations, and procedures as necessary to establish and provide for security measures to: (A) Detect, through electronic, analytical, visual, olfactory, or other means, the presence of weapons; and (B) Aid in the prevention of any individual attempting to unlawfully possess or carry a weapon in any permanent building that is owned by or leased to a local board of education or other public school governing body where students are present in accordance with routine school operations and procedures. (2) Such system, policies, rules, regulations, and procedures shall, at a minimum, require LC 63 0168S buildings, as provided in school safety plans required under Code Section 20-2-1185; provided, however, that such security measures shall not be required for any point of entry to or exit from such permanent buildings that routinely remains locked, is equipped with an alarm that sounds when the point of entry or exit is accessed, and is not intended for student use or is intended for student use only on an emergency basis.\nSECTION 1 (adding O.C.G.A. 20-2-1187(c)): (c) Each local board of education and other public school governing body shall be authorized to use available grants and other funding to meet the requirements of this Code section.\"\nSECTION 2: This Act shall become effective on January 1, 2028."
}